==============================================================================
PART 4 — THE 1/7-SPREAD BOUND:  mu_{1/7}(E) >= thr_k for all integer E (0 in E, |E|=k)
==============================================================================

  (4a) PROVED structural lemmas
   * MONOTONICITY (PROVED): E subset E' => maxgap(E' x)<=maxgap(E x) pointwise
     => {maxgap(E')>θ} ⊆ {maxgap(E)>θ} => mu(E') <= mu(E).
     [VERIFIED consistent] adding a point never raises mu: True
   * SCALE-INVARIANCE (PROVED): mu(gE)=mu(E) (x->x/g pushes Lebesgue to itself).
     [VERIFIED] mu([0, 1, 3, 7, 11]) invariant under scaling: True

  (4b) EXHAUSTIVE bounded-spread (all k-subsets of {0..M}): consec minimizes, none below thr_k
   k=8,M=16: min mu=0.94014 (=consec True), #minimizers=2, below thr_k=0  [thr=0.6185]
   k=9,M=14: min mu=0.84014 (=consec True), #minimizers=1, below thr_k=0  [thr=0.5000]
   k=10,M=14: min mu=0.77551 (=consec True), #minimizers=1, below thr_k=0  [thr=0.3900]

  (4c) seventh-arc-free LOWER BOUND  L7(E) := meas{some open (j/7,(j+1)/7) point-free} <= mu_{1/7}(E)
   k=8: L7(consec)=0.73605  mu=0.94014  thr_k=0.61854  L7>=thr? True
   k=9: L7(consec)=0.65510  mu=0.84014  thr_k=0.50000  L7>=thr? True
   k=10: L7(consec)=0.56179  mu=0.77551  thr_k=0.39000  L7>=thr? True
   k=11: L7(consec)=0.49172  mu=0.62630  thr_k=0.28000  L7>=thr? True
   k=12: L7(consec)=0.42374  mu=0.56990  thr_k=0.14286  L7>=thr? True
   [VERIFIED] on the minimizer L7 already clears thr_k (slack); a uniform proof that
   min_E L7(E) >= thr_k would close the lemma — but min_E L7 is itself at consecutive (same difficulty).

  (4d) huge-spread descent (float, span up to 1e5): large spread RAISES mu toward iid≈1
   tested 220 huge-spread sets; violations(min below consec): 0
   k=8: min mu found=1.0000  consec=0.9402  (>= consec)
   k=9: min mu found=0.9999  consec=0.8401  (>= consec)
   k=10: min mu found=0.9992  consec=0.7755  (>= consec)
   k=11: min mu found=0.9970  consec=0.6263  (>= consec)
   k=12: min mu found=0.9932  consec=0.5699  (>= consec)

  (4e) margin union bound at binding k=8, P={1,5,7,8,9}, E={0..7}:
   delta=0       : meas(G_P^+)=0.38146 mu_(1/7+d)=0.94014 union_bound=+0.32160
   delta=1/140   : meas(G_P^+)=0.33465 mu_(1/7+d)=0.89786 union_bound=+0.23251
   delta=1/280   : meas(G_P^+)=0.35752 mu_(1/7+d)=0.91900 union_bound=+0.27652
   delta=1/560   : meas(G_P^+)=0.36949 mu_(1/7+d)=0.92957 union_bound=+0.29906
   [VERIFIED] ρ*_{1/7+δ} >= meas(G_P^+δ)+mu_{1/7+δ}-1 > 0 for small δ; the margin does NOT break it.

  (4f') L7 reduction target: min_E L7(E) over {0..12}, k=8 (the binding case)
     min L7 = 541/735 = 0.73605 at [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]; #below thr_8=0; thr_8=0.61854
     [VERIFIED EXACT] L7 minimized at consecutive, clears thr_8 with slack 0.1175
     (Paley-Zygmund on the 7-arc partition gives 0.559<thr_8 at k=8 — too lossy; the
      seventh-FREE union L7 itself is the right object, but its min is again consecutive.)

  (4f) STATUS of the spread bound:
   PROVED: monotonicity, scale-invariance, the seventh-free lower bound is valid,
           k<=7 (pigeonhole), k=8 exhaustive over {0..16}.
   VERIFIED (not PROVED): consecutive is the GLOBAL minimizer of mu_{1/7} over ALL integer E,
           hence mu_{1/7}(E) >= mu_{1/7}(consec_k) >= thr_k (binding k=8, slack 0.32).
           Survived exhaustive bounded + huge-spread (1e5) descents; opposite extremizer
           from the FALSE mu_{2/7} (which large spread DROVE below 1/14).
   The residual is a finite-dimensional extremal inequality with large margin; the cleanest
   honest reduction: prove min_E L7(E) >= thr_k (the seventh-free bound), a bounded-denominator
   3-distance computation.  LRC(14) NOT proved.

